```
import React, { useState } from 'react';

const Modal = ({ children, isOpen, onClose }) => {
  const [showModal, setShowModal] = useState(isOpen);

  if (!showModal) {
    return null;
  }

  return (
    <div className="modal">
      <div className="modal-container">
        <div className="modal-header">
          <button className="modal-close" onClick={onClose}>×</button>
        </div>
        <div className="modal-body">{children}</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
};

export default Modal;
```
This component takes three props:

* `children`: the content to be displayed inside the modal
* `isOpen`: a boolean value indicating whether the modal should be displayed
* `onClose`: a function to be called when the user clicks the close button

The component uses the `useState` hook to keep track of whether the modal should be displayed. If `isOpen` is `true`, the component will render the modal content. If `isOpen` is `false`, the component will return `null` and the modal will not be displayed.

The modal container has a header with a close button, and a body that contains the content passed as the `children` prop. When the user clicks the close button, the `onClose` function is called.

You can use this component like this:
```
import React from 'react';
import Modal from './Modal';

const App = () => {
  const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false);

  const closeModal = () => {
    setIsOpen(false);
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <button onClick={() => setIsOpen(true)}>Show Modal</button>
      <Modal isOpen={isOpen} onClose={closeModal}>
        <h2>Hello from the modal!</h2>
        <p>This is some content inside the modal.</p>
      </Modal>
    </div>
  );
};
```
In this example, we create a `Modal` component and pass it two props: `isOpen` and `onClose`. When the user clicks the "Show Modal" button, we set `isOpen` to `true`, which causes the modal to be displayed. When the user clicks the close button inside the modal, we set `isOpen` back to `false`, which causes the modal to be hidden.<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>

